  "description": "Extend the height of the dormer flat roof to obtain 2.5Metre internal height. Internal alterations and associated changes to fenestrations. Conversion of HMO (Use Class C4) to 2No. Self-contained flats (Use Class C3) (Part retrospective)",
  "development_type": "Minor dwellings",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall begin before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.\r\rReason: This is required by Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).",
    "The development to which this permission relates shall be carried out in accordance with the materials specified on the approved plans and on the submitted application form unless otherwise agreed in writing by the local planning authority.\r\rReason: To ensure a satisfactory appearance on completion of the development, in accordance with Policy D3 of the London Plan 2021 and Policies CS8 and DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.",
    "The refuse and recycling facilities as shown on the approved plans shall be provided prior to beneficial occupation of the development to which this permission relates and shall be permanently retained thereafter. The developer and/or their successors in title shall take all reasonable steps to ensure that all refuse and recyclable materials associated with the development are either stored within these facilities or internally within the building(s) on the application site, and that no refuse or recycling material is stored or placed for collection on the public highway except on the day of collection.\r\rReason: To ensure proper waste management in the interests of the character and appearance of the area and the living conditions of neighbouring occupiers, in accordance with policy SI17 of the London Plan 2021 and policies CS8 and DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.",
    "The cycle parking facilities as shown on the approved plans shall be provided prior to beneficial occupation of the development to which this permission relates and shall be permanently retained for that purpose and kept free from obstruction thereafter.\r\rReason: To ensure that appropriate opportunities to promote sustainable transport are taken up, in accordance with policy T5 of the London Plan 2021 and policies CS6 and DM8 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.",
    "The development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved Fire Statement and thereafter maintained. \r\rReason: In the interests of fire safety and to ensure the safety of all building users, in accordance with Policy D12 of the London Plan 2021.",
    "The dwellings hereby approved shall be designed and constructed to achieve a maximum water consumption of no more than 105 litres per person per day (as calculated in accordance with the Building Regulations Optional Requirement G2), and shall thereafter be retained as such.\r\rReason: To ensure the development is sustainable and minimises water consumption in accordance with Policy SI5 of the London Plan (2021) and Policy DM3 of the LDF Core Strategy (2012).",
    "The 2No. car parking spaces shown on the approved drawings  shall be provided and made available for use prior to the first occupation of the dwellings hereby permitted. Thereafter, the parking spaces shall be permanently retained and maintained solely for the parking of private motor vehicles for the occupiers of the residential units hereby approved and their visitors, and for no other purpose.\r\rReason: To ensure that satisfactory provision is made for off-street parking and to remain available for the users of the development, to avoid increased pressure on on-street parking and in the interests of highway safety and the free flow of traffic, in accordance with Policies T6 and T6.1 of the London Plan (2021) and Policy DM9 of the LDF Core Strategy (2012)."
  ],
